cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "OpenVoiceCS-Bench: An Open Benchmark for Voice AI Customer-Service Agents"
message: >-
  If you use OpenVoiceCS-Bench in your research, please cite it using the
  metadata below. Please cite the specific release version together with the
  release-bundle SHA-256 you evaluated against, so results remain traceable to
  a fixed set of artifacts.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Saygili
    given-names: Sezgin
repository-code: "https://github.com/0daycloud/openvoicecs-bench"
abstract: >-
  OpenVoiceCS-Bench evaluates voice AI customer-service agents on whether they
  resolve customer tasks, follow standard operating procedures, use tools
  correctly, protect privacy, preserve authentication boundaries, and refuse
  forbidden actions. Agents emit a replayable trace of messages, tool calls,
  and policy events, which is scored deterministically against a per-scenario
  oracle; subjective conversational quality is scored separately through a
  blinded, multi-rater, adjudicated judging protocol. The v0.1 release contains
  204 synthetic scenarios across six customer-service domains and five tracks
  spanning text, audio, robustness, and adversarial compliance, with
  hash-pinned scenario, split, provenance, judging, and release manifests. v0.1
  is a research preview; see docs/known-limitations.md for measurement
  limitations that currently prevent its scores from being used as a model
  ranking.
keywords:
  - benchmark
  - voice agents
  - customer service
  - conversational ai
  - tool use
  - agent evaluation
  - llm evaluation
  - ai safety
license: Apache-2.0
license-url: "https://github.com/0daycloud/openvoicecs-bench/blob/main/LICENSE"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-06-15"
